# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── secrets
# The API keys. Never commit these, not even to a private repository:
# a private repo can be shared, forked or made public later, and a key in
# history survives all three. configs/ references these by NAME only.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.key
*.pem

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────── the upstream copy
# Dissertation-main/ is a downloaded snapshot of Lagadnakul/Dissertation
# (94 MB). Every file in it already exists in that repository, so committing
# it here would duplicate a whole second repo inside this one. The recovery
# pipeline reads it as convenience, never as the record of truth.
Dissertation-main/

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── deps
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────── scratch and OS
.scratch/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.tmp

# ──────────────────────────────────────────── Word / LaTeX leftovers
~$*.docx
~$*.doc
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc

# ───────────────────────────────────── third-party tooling, not this project
# academic-research-skills/ is a clone of Imbad0202/academic-research-skills
# (70 MB) and carries its own .git. Committing a directory that contains a
# nested repository stores a gitlink, and anyone cloning this project gets an
# empty folder instead. It is a tool used on the work, not part of the work.
# Install it separately:  git clone https://github.com/Imbad0202/academic-research-skills.git ~/academic-research-skills
academic-research-skills/

# .claude/skills/ holds symlinks into .agents/skills/. Git symlinks need
# developer mode on Windows and silently become text files without it, so the
# real skill content is committed under .agents/ and each machine makes its
# own links (see SETUP.md).
.claude/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Dissertation-main/ is the ORIGINAL experiment tree, restored from the pinned
# provenance commit (Lagadnakul/Dissertation @ c8872d07 — a dangling commit, not
# reachable from main, which has since been replaced). Two tests in
# tests/promptOracle.test.ts hash four of its day*.py files to prove the
# committed prompt templates still match the Python they were extracted from.
#
# Not committed, for the same reason as archive/legacy_*: an immutable upstream
# sha beats a duplicate in the repository. Rebuild it with the recipe in
# recovery-bench/archive/MANIFEST.md.
Dissertation-main/

# The taste-skill's working directory: the dealt sheet and the inspector's
# screenshots at 1440/768/390, rewritten on every run. Not committed, because
# the only part worth keeping is the seed, and that is written into
# DASHBOARD.md §2 — `draw.mjs --show` reprints the sheet from it.
.taste-skill/
